    "body": "2026 Paris Motor Show • 1971 Nissan Skyline 2000GT-R Is Now an 833-Piece Mattel Brick Shop Set That Can Be Customized\nToyota Motor Europe Posts Record Nine-Month Sales, Celebrates With Corolla 60th Anniversary Editions\n10 photos\nPhoto: Toyota Europe\nToyota Motor Europe (TME) , the local subsidiary of the world's largest automaker, Toyota Motor Corporation, has announced its nine-month sales tally for the Old Continent.\nToyota Motor Europe (TME) announced a new record for its Old Continent sales of 936,042 units for the namesake Toyota and the premium Lexus brands during the first nine months of 2026, up a mere 0.6%. The company continues to post its highest strength across the electrified field, with the latter segment accounting for 87% of total sales or 813,623 deliveries.\nDuring the time, battery electric vehicle sales more than doubled to 104,832 units, jumping 136% year-on-year, driven by “strong customer demand” for the Toyota C-HR+, bZ4X, Urban Cruiser, and bZ4X Touring. Lexus, unfortunately, can’t be happy about the performance: it sold 62,597 units from January through September 2026, which is down four percentage points compared to last year.\nOn the other hand, the namesake Toyota brand managed to compensate and reached 873,445 deliveries, up almost one percentage point. The electrified sales reached 753,665 units and soared by 15%, while the Toyota Professional series, aka the Hilux and Proace families, were at over 113k units.\n“Customers are responding strongly to our electrified line-up, with notable growth across both hybrid and battery electric vehicles. The Aygo X Hybrid, introduced last year, is bringing our hybrid technology to more customers, while the Toyota C-HR+, bZ4X and bZ4X Touring are driving our growing BEV presence in Europe,” explains Till Conrad, Executive Vice President – Sales, Toyota Motor Europe.\nThe new Toyota RAV4 Hybrid and PHEV is going well with 41,697 sales, but the Aygo X, Yaris, C-HR, and Corolla still sold better across Europe. Speaking of the Corolla series, the nameplate celebrates 60 years in 2026 and has sold almost one million vehicles per year, each year, with current all-time deliveries standing at 57 million units and counting.\nToday, the Toyota Corolla models are produced at 14 production centers in 11 countries, and the 12th generation consists of hatchback, sedan, and Touring Sports (station wagon) models, plus the related Corolla Cross compact crossover SUV. Unsurprisingly, Toyota says it kept the same recipe all these years, and only adapted it to the current times.\n“Corolla’s sustained success is founded on the principles that Toyota applied in creating the original model back in 1966. The vision then was for a high-quality, versatile car at an affordable price. Today, 12 generations later, it remains true to those qualities, having constantly adapted over the years to maintain its place at the heart of the market,” explains the company.\nIn Europe, the Toyota Corolla was first produced beginning in 1971 from complete knock-down kits and full-scale manufacturing began in 1994, with almost 9.5 million sales originating from the Old Continent. Today, production is located at Toyota Motor Manufacturing UK for the Corolla hatchback and Touring Sports, while the sedan is manufactured by Toyota Motor Manufacturing Turkey.\nAdditionally, the company celebrates six decades of achievements with the European-built Hatchback, Touring Sports and Sedan 60th anniversary limited edition models . The 60th Anniversary versions of the Hatchback and Touring Sports, built in the UK, have a new and exclusive Boreal Blue metallic paint, presented in a dual-tone style with a contrasting Night Sky Black roof and pillars.\nThere are also new 17-inch alloy wheels with a contrast matt and machined finish, while the Corolla Sedan gains its own signature Lunar Sky Blue paint and shares the 17-inch wheels, 60th Anniversary badging, scuff plates and carpet mats with its sibling Hatchback and Touring Sports models.\nLiked the article? Follow us to see more articles from autoevolution in your Google feeds.\nToyota Toyota Corolla Corolla sales Europe 60th anniversary TME toyota motor europe\nAbout the author: Aurel Niculescu\nAurel has aimed high all his life (literally, at 16 he was flying gliders all by himself) so in 2006 he switched careers and got hired as a writer at his favorite magazine. Since then, his work has been published both by print and online outlets, most recently right here, on autoevolution. Full profile\nUP NEXT BMW’s i3 Touring Is an Electric Alternative to the Upcoming 3 Series Wagon – Spy Shots",
